From: f <f@f>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: videocc-sm8450: Let the VPU control the mvs0 core clock

The video encoder firmware (vpu20_4v) is told by the driver that the
hardware may power collapse the VPP core on its own (HFI_PROP_
INTRA_FRAME_POWER_COLLAPSE), and the mvs0 power domain already allows
the hardware trigger (HW_CTRL_TRIGGER). The third piece of that path is
the clock: the VPU can only restart its own core clock when the RCG is
in hardware clock control mode (CFG_HW_CLK_CTRL, bit 20 of the CFG
register). The downstream videocc-waipio driver sets it on
video_cc_mvs0_clk_src (HW_CLK_CTRL_MODE); mainline knows the mode
(struct clk_rcg2::hw_clk_ctrl) but no clock source on SM8450 enables
it.

Without it the VPP never comes back once the encoder firmware hands
the core to the hardware, and the first encoded frame resets the whole
SoC. Decoding does not enter that path and worked regardless.

Local Diting bring-up change, not submitted upstream.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8450.c	2026-11-23 19:51:06.740830377 +0800
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8450.c	2026-11-23 19:51:06.740830377 +0800
@@ -156,6 +156,7 @@
 	.hid_width = 5,
 	.parent_map = video_cc_parent_map_0,
 	.freq_tbl = ftbl_video_cc_mvs0_clk_src,
+	.hw_clk_ctrl = true,
 	.clkr.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
 		.name = "video_cc_mvs0_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = video_cc_parent_data_0,
